WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.435
The Design phase turns analysis into a learning plan.

2
00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:19.922
This is where course creators define learning objectives, performance outcomes, module sequence, instructional strategy, examples, practice opportunities, assessment approach, narration plan, visual direction, and accessibility expectations.

3
00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:27.325
The design should explain how the course will help learners move from current performance to desired performance.

4
00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:31.829
Learning objectives should be specific enough to guide development.

5
00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:37.095
A vague objective such as understand the policy is hard to teach and hard to assess.

6
00:00:37.095 --> 00:00:44.652
A stronger objective describes what learners will be able to identify, choose, apply, compare, perform, or explain.

7
00:00:44.652 --> 00:00:54.346
The objective becomes a filter for content: if a detail does not support the objective, it may belong in a reference document instead of the main course.

8
00:00:54.346 --> 00:00:56.101
Course structure matters.

9
00:00:56.101 --> 00:01:01.902
Modules should build in a logical order, usually from context to concepts to application.

10
00:01:01.902 --> 00:01:04.650
Examples make abstract content concrete.

11
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:10.146
Practice gives learners a chance to use the information before the final assessment.

12
00:01:10.146 --> 00:01:15.336
Assessments should measure the same knowledge or decisions the course teaches.

13
00:01:15.336 --> 00:01:23.885
Alignment is the core design discipline: objectives, content, practice, media, and assessment should point in the same direction.

14
00:01:23.885 --> 00:01:28.770
Storyboards make the design visible before production becomes expensive.

15
00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:35.639
A storyboard can show screen flow, narration, visual ideas, interactions, feedback, and quiz alignment.

16
00:01:35.639 --> 00:01:43.883
It gives stakeholders something to review before the team records audio, builds complex interactions, or creates final media.

17
00:01:43.883 --> 00:01:49.683
A storyboard is not busywork; it is a way to catch problems while they are still cheap to fix.

18
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:53.500
Accessibility should be planned here, not added at the end.

19
00:01:53.500 --> 00:02:03.728
Decisions about captions, transcripts, keyboard navigation, alt text, reading order, contrast, plain language, and media alternatives all affect design.

20
00:02:03.728 --> 00:02:09.376
A strong design phase makes the learner experience clearer before development begins.
